# .toolignore: files and folders codewhy should not document.
#
# Syntax is the same as .gitignore: one pattern per line, `#` starts a comment,
# a trailing `/` matches folders only, `*` and `**` are wildcards, and a leading
# `!` re-includes something an earlier pattern excluded.
#
# codewhy never reads .gitignore. A file you ignore from git (generated code,
# local scripts) is still documented unless it is listed here.
#
# Built-in ignores always apply before this file: node_modules/ .venv/ venv/
# __pycache__/ .git/ dist/ build/ .next/ *.min.js *.d.ts .pytest_cache/
# .mypy_cache/ .idea/ .vscode/
#
# To document a folder a built-in ignores, re-include it. For example, if your
# own source code lives in build/:
# !build/
#
# Note: you cannot re-include a single file inside an ignored folder
# (`!build/keep.py` has no effect while build/ itself is ignored), same as git.
#
# codewhy's own files (.codewhy/, the output folder, PROJECT_DOCS.md,
# codewhy.toml, .toolignore) are always excluded and cannot be re-included.

# Examples:
# tests/fixtures/
# *.generated.ts
